# No Secrets in Tests

Never hardcode credentials, tokens, or environment-specific URLs in specs, page objects, or fixtures.

## Rules

- Read secrets from `process.env` (or a small config helper that reads env). Put local values in `.env` and keep `.env` gitignored.
- Set `use.baseURL` in `playwright.config.ts`. Specs and page objects use paths (`/login`), not full hostnames.
- Test users, API tokens, and third-party keys belong in CI secrets / env, not in source.
- Do not commit `.env`, credential JSON, or `playwright/.auth` files that contain real sessions.
- Placeholders in examples must stay obviously fake (`user@example.com`) or come from env.

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
await loginPage.login('real-user@company.com', 'ProdPassword123!');
await page.goto('https://staging.company.com/login');

// ✅ GOOD
await loginPage.goto(); // page.goto('/login') inside the page object
await loginPage.login(process.env.TEST_USER_EMAIL!, process.env.TEST_USER_PASSWORD!);
```
